{#- The user message of every structured decision (`grimoire.inference.structured_messages`).
    Vars:
      items   — [decisions.Item]: each its `context` (text) and its ordered
                `questions`. A question's `KIND` says what it is: a Predicate
                ("predicate": `id`, `instructions`), a Choice ("choice": also
                `options`, each `id` and `description`, and `allow_none`), a
                Score ("score": also `levels`, ordered descriptions), a Rank
                ("rank": also `candidates`, each `id` and `description`, `top`
                and `allow_none`) or a MultiSelect ("select": also `options`,
                `min`, `max` and `allow_none`; a bound renders only when it is
                set, `max` of 0 included). The branches test `KIND`, never which
                attributes a question has. Option `aliases` are the parser's
                and are never shown, nor is a rank's `pointwise` (a native
                stage's alone).
      explain — str: the rationale instruction ("" when none is asked for). -#}
{%- for item in items %}
{%- if not loop.first %}

{% endif -%}
Item {{ loop.index0 }}

{{ item.context }}

Questions:
{%- for q in item.questions %}
{%- if q.KIND == "choice" %}
- {{ q.id }} (choice{% if q.allow_none %}, or null for none of these{% endif %}): {{ q.instructions }}
{%- for opt in q.options %}
  - {{ opt.id }}: {{ opt.description }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- elif q.KIND == "score" %}
- {{ q.id }} (scale): {{ q.instructions }}
{%- for level in q.levels %}
  - {{ loop.index0 }}: {{ level }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- elif q.KIND == "rank" %}
- {{ q.id }} (ranking, best first{% if q.top is not none %}, at least the top {{ q.top }}{% endif %}{% if q.allow_none %}, or null if they cannot be ordered{% endif %}): {{ q.instructions }}
{%- for opt in q.candidates %}
  - {{ opt.id }}: {{ opt.description }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- elif q.KIND == "select" %}
- {{ q.id }} (selection{% if q.min %}, at least {{ q.min }}{% endif %}{% if q.max is not none %}, at most {{ q.max }}{% endif %}{% if q.allow_none %}, or null if it cannot be said{% endif %}): {{ q.instructions }}
{%- for opt in q.options %}
  - {{ opt.id }}: {{ opt.description }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- else %}
- {{ q.id }} (yes/no): {{ q.instructions }}
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- if explain %}

Rationale, for each item: {{ explain }}
{%- endif %}
